Weekly security posture audit at 04:00 AM ET on Sundays.

Read `_Iris_Memory/Sessions/CLAUDE_CODE_HANDOFF.md` (latest entry) for context. Hard rules from `06_CEO/Designs/2026-05-26_Claude_Code_Engineering_Handoff.md` apply.

**Dispatch the `security-auditor` subagent** (via the Task tool) to run a FULL live audit. Its complete operating spec lives in `/Users/steve/.claude/agents/security-auditor.md` — it knows the method; do not re-specify it. Pass the subagent a prompt that says: run a full live security posture audit now as a SCHEDULED routine — execute every axis (vault secret-leak sweep, git-history scan across iris-studio AND every repo under ~/iris_mcps, credential-file permissions including the .bak stale-token copies, public-network/tunnel exposure, Syncthing state, launchd com.iris.* integrity, light dependency check); write the dated report to `/Users/steve/Documents/3SK/outputs/06_CEO/Security_Audits/YYYY-MM-DD_security_audit.md` (today's ISO date); append the verdict + any 🔴/🟠 lines to `/Users/steve/Documents/3SK/outputs/INBOX.md` via `cat >>`; fire `scripts/notify.sh` for CONFIRMED criticals only; redact every secret to last-4 in both the report and any alert.

When the subagent returns, read its summary and decide the completion signal below from its `status:` and verdict.

**Transcribe any PATTERN CANDIDATE it emitted (added 2026-07-29).** `security-auditor` carries the pattern-candidate block, and its reply comes back to YOU in this transcript — it never lands in a vault file, so the harvest cannot see it and the lesson is lost. Scan its returned report for lines naming `PATTERN CANDIDATE` and append each one **VERBATIM, byte-for-byte** to today's daily note under a `### 🧪 Pattern candidates emitted` heading placed at the **very END of the daily note**, after every existing agent section (create it if absent) — never mid-file inside another agent's section. **Append to that heading, never rewrite it** — the nightly `vault-gardener` writes the same heading, and it starts at 04:10 while this job starts at 04:00, so on a Sunday you may well still be composing when it runs. Replacing the section would delete its transcribed markers before the harvest ever sees them, which is the 2026-07-29 loss all over again. Read the section, add your lines, leave everything else byte-identical. Do NOT paraphrase, summarise or count-only: a summary of a marker is not a marker, which is exactly how the 2026-07-29 gardener lost one. Copy a malformed line verbatim anyway — the harvest reports those loudly, and that is how the emitting agent gets fixed. State the count in your report ("transcribed N marker line(s)", including 0), so a skipped step is distinguishable from "nothing was emitted". Do NOT run the harvest here — the nightly vault-gardener owns that.

**Drift watch (do NOT duplicate the monthly credential-check):** this audit owns posture/exposure; the 1st-of-month `credential-check` routine owns rotation-age. If the auditor surfaces something rotation-age-shaped, note it but don't re-rank — that's the other routine's lane.

**Bridge file:** append a 2-line bridge summary to `_Iris_Memory/Sessions/CLAUDE_CODE_HANDOFF.md` ONLY if the verdict is 🔴 EXPOSED or any 🟠 high was found. Skip for a clean ✅ SECURE week.

**Append to today's daily note (per-agent-sections convention).** After your primary task, append ONE bullet to `_Iris_Memory/Daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (today's ISO date) under the `## 🤖 Claude Code intra-day log` section. Format: `HH:MM — security audit → <verdict>, <n> findings (report path)`. If the daily note doesn't exist yet, create it from `01_Operating_Docs/Templates/Daily_Note_Template.md` and fill the frontmatter date/day fields. Do NOT edit Cowork's `## 📝 Cowork-Iris intra-day log` section.

---

## ⛳ Completion signal — REQUIRED LAST LINE (run_claude_job.sh reads this for Steve's Telegram alert)

After all other work and logging, the VERY LAST line of your output MUST be exactly one of:
- `ROUTINE_COMPLETE` — the audit ran and the report was written. NOTE: a 🔴 EXPOSED or ⚠️ HARDEN verdict is still `ROUTINE_COMPLETE` — the *audit itself* succeeded; the findings are the deliverable, not a routine failure.
- `ROUTINE_INCOMPLETE: <one-line reason>` — the audit could not run or was only partial (subagent returned `status: blocked-*` / `partial-*`, a path was inaccessible, or a step was skipped).

Do NOT echo the subagent's full report as your final output — your last line must be the bare sentinel and nothing after it (the wrapper reads only the parent's last line). Output nothing after that line. This line is how Steve gets a done / not-fully-done alert on Telegram.
